  "slug": "phases-symtft-1132",
  "summary": "Preprints extend topological and magnetic classification to half-chiral symmetry, spin space groups and fractal lattices.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is symmetry-constrained classification: the controlling symmetry, invariant or lattice setting is widened, and the resulting phases or magnetic orders are then enumerated or characterized accordingly. One preprint treats topological phases protected by half-chiral symmetry, where chiral symmetry acts on a single sublattice, using real-space invariants and zero-energy modes. A second enumerates spin space groups via translation holonomy, yielding 17 spin-lattice types with neutron diffraction signatures; this classifies magnetic order rather than topological phases. A third realizes SSH, Haldane, Qi-Wu-Zhang and Z2 insulators on fractal lattices such as the Cantor set, hexaflake and Sierpiński carpet, including site-eliminated, projected and patterned constructions. What is new is the extension of protecting symmetries, invariants and lattice geometries rather than a single shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
